Release 5 / Serial number 250524 / Inform v6.43 Library 6/11 S

Image Room
A voice booooms out: Try "image" for a sample of alignments, or "image NUMBER", or "image NUMBER ALIGN". Alignments are "up", "down", "center", "left", "right". Throw in the word "caption" to mix some text on the line. Throw in "link" to make the image a hyperlink. Adding a term like "100x200" will scale the image to those dimensions.

Try "scales" for a sample of scaling options. For more control, use "image" with "wfix", "worig", "wratio", "hfix", "horig", "hratio". Ratio scales are written like "1/1x3/2". (Note that "1/1" is interpreted as $10000, not 1 -- ratios are 16x16 fixed-point.)

You can set the width max with "maxwidth" (100% window width) or "halfwidth" (50%). These are the only options at present.

You can also type "size NUMBER" to check an image size. Type "text" for a long text paragraph, "clear" to clear the text buffer, and "break" for a flow break.

Images that should be available (imported from Sensory Jam): 0, 1, 2, 5, 10, 11.

>size 0
Image 0 size: 125 by 180.

>size 1
Image 1 size: 150 by 180.

>size 2
Image 2 size: 155 by 180.

>size 5
Image 5 size: 47 by 62.

>size 10
Image 10 size: 128 by 128.

>size 11
Image 11 size: 128 by 128.

>size 3
There is no image 3.

>image
Here are several images in a row:
With inlineup: [image 0 up 125x180] With inlinedown: [image 10 down 128x128] With inlinecenter: [image 5 center 47x62]

